    "id": 6,
    "title": "The average three-dimensional supergranule in numerical simulations",
    "description": "Supergranulation is one of the Sun’s dominant convective patterns, but its subsurface extent remains unknown. In this project, you will analyse pre-computed 3D hydrodynamic simulations of near-surface solar convection to reconstruct an average supergranule and track its evolution with depth. By identifying, aligning, and averaging a number of simulated cells, you will uncover the hidden subsurface structure of supergranulation: how its characteristic outflows change with depth. You will work with large simulation datasets, develop statistical and visualisation techniques, and compare your results with helioseismic observations of the Sun. This project offers a chance to investigate a fundamental open question in solar physics using modern computational tools, and would suit a physics, maths or engineering student.",
