    "id": 9,
    "title": "Measuring the rotation of Sun-like stars",
    "description": "Stellar rotation provides a window into magnetic activity, stellar age, and the transport of angular momentum inside stars. ESA’s PLATO mission will observe thousands of stars, creating an unprecedented opportunity to measure how rotation varies across Sun-like stars. In this project, you will obtain PLATO light curves for FGK-type stars and develop a Python pipeline to measure their rotation periods using the Lomb–Scargle periodogram. You will identify significant periodic signals, assess their reliability, and investigate how the measured rotation periods depend on stellar type, activity, and data quality. Where possible, you will compare the results with independent rotation measurements and examine the distribution of rotation rates across the sample. The project will provide hands-on experience with astronomical time-series data, Fourier and Lomb–Scargle methods, statistical significance testing, and scientific programming. The resulting rotation catalogue will help characterise the magnetic and rotational evolution of Sun-like stars.",
