    "title": "Rad on Rails - Investigating the need for mobile radiotherapy in rural areas",
    "description": "For many rural Australians, the long travel requirements to metropolitan cancer treatment centres means that some people are unable to (or choose not to) receive radiotherapy treatment, resulting in decreased survival with increased remoteness. One potential solution is to deploy mobile radiotherapy units to rural areas transported by either truck or train. Doing so would be the first of its kind in Australia, and therefore requires substantial planning before the construction of the unit can commence. The proposed project would involve the student assessing the needs and preferences of rural patients, developing schedules, identifying suitable locations, and aligning the project with existing services, like mobile chemotherapy clinics.",
