    "id": 26,
    "title": "Investigating clinical practices regarding the SEAFARER spine PSQA audit",
    "description": "This project aims to improve the safety of radiotherapy cancer treatment in Australia and internationally by building on the SEAFARER remote patient-specific quality assurance (PSQA) audits. The SEAFARER project investigates the sensitivity and specificity of dosimetry measurements performed in radiotherapy clinics. It gives physicists at those clinics an opportunity to check their methods and to compare their results to those of others around the world. SEAFARER uses a cloud-based platform allowing participants to obtain the needed information, submit their data and receive feedback, including comparisons to others, in real time. The student would design and conduct follow-up surveys/interviews with centres who completed a recent SEAFARER audit to answer the questions: what aspects of clinical practices are influential in PSQA performance and what impact the audit has had on current radiotherapy practices. This provides opportunity for a student to communicate and build connections with many radiotherapy centres across Australia and gain insight into current clinical PSQA practices which may be ideal for a student considering pursuing TEAP in the future.",
