    "title": "Full-spectrum analysis of atom probe tomography mass-to-charge-ratio spectra",
    "description": "Atom probe tomography combines a field ion microscope with time-of-flight mass spectroscopy system to provide 3D, near-atomic-scale microanalysis of solid samples. Specimen chemistry is found by summing ranges around peaks in the mass-to-charge ratio spectrum. This involves arbitrary decisions about peak extent, leading to different measured compositions depending on the protocol used, and disagreement in the community about best-practices. Inspired by analysis of X-ray diffraction patterns, this project will analyse the peaks in atom probe mass-to-charge ratio spectra to develop (a) a useful peak-shape model, and (b) a full-spectrum fit to provide very accurate compositional measurements. The researcher will primarily be writing code (in Python, or a language of their choice) to apply to existing datasets, but there is opportunity to collect new atom probe data at the University of Sydney. This project is well-suited to a researcher with a background in physics, programming, and mathematics.",
